|Has anyone tried this?

I tried it under DOS.   What happened was that I copied a bones.25 to bones.2.
Then I played a number of times, just running for the stairs down.  Eventually
I got the following message:
"This dungeon doesn't look like I remembered it . . . --more
	Do you wish to see your inventory when you died? (y/n)"
And in the highscore list:
"Killed by trickery."

Then I tried scanning the bones file for a string along the lines of "25",
which would be an obvious method of saving what level it is supposed to be.
No such luck.  Ah, well.  Looks like you just have to die on level 2 with
your kick-ass character for your next character to reap the spoils.

So much for that abuse.

